// An integer instance converts to its integer and a string instance to its string where a value is needed; an instance used as a condition means that it holds; an integer used as a condition means it is at least 1.
Fact x Identified by Int
Fact s Identified by String.
+x(5). +s(Hi).
?(x + 1 == 6).
?(s == Hi).
?x(5).
?1. ?!0. ?!(0-1). ?2.
